    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "In computing and computer science, a processor or processing unit is an
    electrical component (digital circuit) that performs operations on an external
    data source, usually memory or some other data stream.[1] It typically takes
    the form of a microprocessor, which can be implemented on a single or a few tightly
    integrated metal\u2013oxide\u2013semiconductor integrated circuit chips.[2][3]
    In the past, processors were constructed using multiple individual vacuum tubes,[4][5]
    multiple individual transistors,[6] or multiple integrated circuits."
